# BuildKit reads <dockerfile>.dockerignore in preference to .dockerignore, so the
# container build context is scoped here without touching the repository root.
# Allow-list: only what the image actually needs.
*

!easybfe
!environment.yml
!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!LICENSE
!container

# ... minus everything under container/ that is not a build input.
#
# container/e2e-abfe-test is excluded on purpose: test systems, configs and results
# never enter the image. They are mounted at run time instead, so changing a
# test case does not change the image.
container/e2e-abfe-test
container/Amber26.pdf
container/DEVELOP.md
container/README.md

**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
**/.DS_Store
